{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774329538,"nonce":"5MAVJW+mJME22qMIm2fV/6Xw8S0=","message":"## Implementation Spec\n\n### Files to create\n- `feedbax/web/api/analyses.py` — GET /api/analyses/packages\n- `feedbax/web/api/runs.py` — GET /api/runs/training, GET /api/runs/training/{id}/evals\n\n### Files to modify\n- `feedbax/web/app.py` — register new routers\n\n### GET /api/analyses/packages\nReturns `{ packages: AnalysisPackage[] }` matching frontend TS type.\n\nImplementation:\n1. Import EXPERIMENT_REGISTRY from feedbax.plugins\n2. Iterate registry.get_package_names() and their parts\n3. For each part, load the analysis module via registry.get_analysis_module(f\"{part}\")\n4. Introspect module-level ANALYSES dict (if present): each value is an AbstractAnalysis instance\n5. For each analysis: extract name (class name), docstring -\u003e description, Ports fields -\u003e inputPorts, fig_params keys -\u003e defaultParams, category from package/part name\n6. Output ports: from the analysis class itself (inferred from compute/make_figs return annotations or hardcoded as [\"data\"]/[\"figure\"])\n7. The frontend gracefully falls back to STUB_PACKAGES on failure\n\nSince analysis modules live in experiment packages (not feedbax core) and may not be installed, wrap the entire introspection in try/except and return empty list on failure. The endpoint is discovery-only; it never imports JAX or runs analysis code.\n\nHowever: the analysis classes in feedbax/analysis/*.py ARE the classes referenced by the stub data (Violins, StatesPCA, etc.). The experiment package modules just compose instances of these classes into ANALYSES dicts. The introspection should work at the class level (AbstractAnalysis subclasses), examining their Ports ClassVar and fig_params defaults.\n\nApproach: iterate installed packages, for each part try loading the analysis module, extract ANALYSES dict, introspect each instance. Category = package part name. Input ports = dataclass field names on the Ports class. Output ports = [\"figure\"] if make_figs is overridden, [\"data\"] otherwise. Default params = dict(fig_params). Icon = \"\" (frontend can supply defaults).\n\n### GET /api/runs/training\nReturns `TrainingRun[]` (snake_case wire: id, name, created_at, status, hyperparams).\n\nImplementation:\n1. Query ModelRecord grouped by expt_name\n2. Each group = one \"training run\"\n3. id = model hash (first/representative), name = expt_name, created_at = earliest timestamp\n4. status = \"completed\" (all records are post-training)\n5. hyperparams = extract key columns (model__n_replicates, pert__type, pert__std, n_batches) from the representative record\n\n### GET /api/runs/training/{training_run_id}/evals\nReturns `EvalRun[]`.\n\nImplementation:\n1. training_run_id = model hash\n2. Query EvaluationRecord where model_hashes contains the given hash\n3. Map to EvalRun: id = eval hash, training_run_id, name = expt_name or eval hash prefix, created_at, status = \"completed\", description from perturbation_config summary","files":null}]}